            <ArticleTitle>Report of the International Society for Zinc Biology 5th Meeting, in Collaboration with Zinc-Net (COST Action TD1304)-UCLan Campus, Pyla, Cyprus.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E2518</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/ijms18122518</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>From 18 to 22 June 2017, the fifth biennial meeting of the International Society for Zinc Biology was held in conjunction with the final dissemination meeting of the Network for the Biology of Zinc (Zinc-Net) at the University of Central Lancashire, Cyprus campus. The meeting attracted over 160 participants, had 17 scientific symposia, 4 plenary speakers and 2 poster discussion sessions. In this report, we give an overview of the key themes of the meeting and some of the highlights from the scientific programme.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
